  "investigation_notes": "Upload investigation - current state unclear / `insufficient_evidence` for persistent root-cause.\n\n**What was observed:**\n\n* Both containers `running` at check time: `incidentlab-app-1 Up 6 seconds`, `incidentlab-db-1 Up 11 seconds (healthy)` (E1).\n* App `/health` returns `200 {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2). DB `healthy`, `running true`, `restart_count 0`, `oom_killed false` (E10), `ready to accept connections` with no errors (E8). App also `running true`, `exit_code 0`, `oom_killed false`, `restart_count 0` (E7).\n* App log shows upload failure symptom: `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` with `File \"/app/main.py\", line 59, in upload out.write(chunk) OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` (E3)(E12).\n* Same log shows successes before and after that failure: `POST /upload 200 OK` + `GET /files/... 200 OK` + `DELETE /files/... 200 OK` before failure, and `POST /upload 200 OK` + `GET /files/... 200 OK` + `DELETE /files/... 200 OK` after failure (E3)(E12). `/health 200 OK` also continues after (E12).\n* `recent_events` shows no app `die/stop/oom/kill/restart`, only `start` at `23:40:38` (E9). DB health checks `exec_die exit 0` and `health_status: healthy` throughout (E9).\n\n**What was ruled out as persistent cause:**\n\n* Persistent capacity exhaustion on upload filesystem ruled out: `/srv/lab-data mountpoint /srv/lab-data size_mb 487.2 used_mb 40.7 available_mb 410.7 use_percent 9.0` (E4).\n* Persistent inode exhaustion ruled out: `/srv/lab-data inode_use_percent 0.2` (E4), `/ inode_use_percent 1.5` (E5).\n* Root filesystem full ruled out: `/ size_mb 98121.7 used_mb 6680.4 available_mb 91425.4 use_percent 6.8` (E5).\n* Permission denied as cause ruled out: `/srv/lab-data/uploads is_dir true owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app 1000:1000 app_user_can_write true` (E6), parent `/srv/lab-data is_dir true owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app_user_can_write true` (E11), and app runs as `1000:1000` (E7) with bind `source /srv/lab-data destination /data rw true` (E7).\n* DB dependency failure ruled out as cause of that `upload` exception: DB `healthy` (E10)(E1), logs ready (E8), no DB error lines (E8).\n\n**Why `insufficient_evidence`:**\n\n* Direct symptom evidence is `ENOSPC on out.write` (E3)(E12), but current capacity/inode evidence shows ample free space (E4)(E5) and writability (E6)(E11).\n* Failure was single/transient in log sequence, with `200 OK` uploads immediately before and after (E3)(E12), and current health `200` (E2). No evidence in collected checks shows which filesystem/file filled, quota, tmpfs, deleted-but-open file, or other `ENOSPC` source.\n* Per rule not to conclude a cause only by elimination, persistent `disk-full` / `permission` / `db` cannot be asserted. No repair action justified. Needs deeper host-level check: exact write path in `main.py`, `df -h` for `/tmp`/`/dev/shm`/overlay inside container, quotas, `lsof | deleted`.\n",
